CAMERA SYSTEM — STRONG IMPACT-SHAKE PHYSICS
Camera reacts to every action with physically simulated impulses. Always grounded — never random.
Shake Types
Distant explosions: low-frequency rumble sway (1–2 Hz), subtle roll
Near artillery impacts: mid-frequency vertical kick (4–7 Hz), 3–5 frame punch
Tracers near lens: high-frequency micro-vibrations (12–18 Hz)
Shockwave blasts: camera pushed backward with elastic delay
Debris impacts: single-frame jolt + 40–60 ms stabilization
Inertia Model
Camera behaves like a 5–7 kg steadicam:
delayed recovery
sliding momentum on uneven terrain
slight rolling oscillation after large shocks
Directional Response
Explosion left → jolt right + clockwise roll
Explosion right → jolt left + counterclockwise roll
Shockwave frontal → backward push + rumbling decay
Splash below → upward kick

